OpenChat Feature Parity & Enhancement Plan

  Current State Summary

  ✅ What's Working Well:
  - Channels (public/private) with full CRUD
  - Direct Messages (1-on-1 and group)
  - Real-time messaging via WebSockets + Redis Pub/Sub
  - Message threading infrastructure (backend ready)
  - Reactions, typing indicators, user presence
  - Multi-org isolation with PostgreSQL RLS
  - Horizontal scaling capability

  ❌ Critical Gaps:
  - No end-to-end encryption
  - Missing: search, mentions, notifications, attachments
  - Thread UI not implemented
  - No unread tracking or read receipts
  - Limited permission granularity
  - No message pinning, bookmarks, or rich formatting

  ---
  Proposed Implementation Plan

  Phase 1: Foundation & Critical UX Features (Priority 1)

  1.1 Unread Message Tracking & Notifications
  - Add channel_read_status and dm_read_status tables
    - Track last_read_message_id and last_read_at per user
    - Add unread_count column (denormalized for performance)
  - Add notifications table for mention/DM alerts
  - UI: Unread badges on channels/DMs in sidebar
  - API:
    - POST /api/channels/{id}/read - Mark as read
    - GET /api/channels/{id}/unread - Get unread count
    - GET /api/notifications - List notifications

  1.2 Message Search (Full-Text)
  - Create PostgreSQL GIN index on messages.content with tsvector
  - Add to_tsvector trigger for automatic indexing
  - API: GET /api/search/messages?q={query}&scope={channel|dm|all}
  - UI: Global search bar with keyboard shortcut (Cmd/Ctrl+K)
  - Support filters: from:@user, in:#channel, before:date, after:date

  1.3 File Attachments
  - S3 integration for file storage (pre-signed URLs)
  - API handlers:
    - POST /api/attachments/upload - Get pre-signed S3 URL
    - POST /api/attachments - Save attachment metadata
    - DELETE /api/attachments/{id} - Delete attachment
  - Support images (inline preview), documents, videos
  - File size limits and type validation
  - Virus scanning integration (ClamAV or AWS GuardDuty)

  1.4 @Mentions & Channel Notifications
  - Parse message content for @username and @channel
  - Add mentions table (message_id, mentioned_user_id, type)
  - Create notifications when mentioned
  - UI: Highlight mentions, auto-complete @ suggestions
  - API: GET /api/mentions - List user's mentions

  1.5 Thread Display UI
  - Build ThreadPanel.tsx component (already exists but incomplete)
  - Show thread count on parent messages
  - Inline thread preview (first reply + count)
  - Side panel for full thread view
  - Notifications for thread replies

  ---
  Phase 2: End-to-End Encryption (Priority 1 - Can run parallel with Phase 1)

  2.1 E2E Encryption Architecture
  - Protocol: Signal Protocol (or Matrix Olm/Megolm for group chats)
  - Key Strategy:
    - Per-user identity key pair (Ed25519)
    - Per-device signing keys
    - One-time prekeys for forward secrecy
    - Ratcheting for message-level keys

  2.2 Database Schema Changes
  - Add user_devices table:
    - device_id, user_id, identity_key, signing_key, prekeys[], last_seen
  - Add encrypted_channels table:
    - channel_id, encryption_enabled, algorithm, megolm_session_id
  - Modify messages table:
    - Add encrypted_content (BYTEA)
    - Add encryption_metadata (JSONB) - algorithm, sender_device_id, session_id
    - Keep content NULL for encrypted messages

  2.3 Key Management Service
  - API endpoints:
    - POST /api/crypto/devices - Register device
    - GET /api/crypto/devices/{user_id} - Get user's devices
    - POST /api/crypto/prekeys - Upload prekeys
    - GET /api/crypto/prekeys/{user_id} - Fetch prekeys for encryption
    - POST /api/crypto/session - Establish encryption session

  2.4 Encryption Implementation
  - Rust Backend:
    - Add vodozemac crate (Rust implementation of Olm/Megolm)
    - Or use libsignal-protocol-rust
    - Server only stores encrypted blobs, never has plaintext
  - Frontend:
    - Add @matrix-org/olm or libsignal-client-web
    - Encrypt messages before sending to WebSocket/API
    - Decrypt on receipt in client
    - IndexedDB for local key storage

  2.5 UI for E2E Encryption
  - Channel settings: "Enable End-to-End Encryption"
  - Device verification flow (compare safety numbers)
  - Lock icon on encrypted messages
  - Key backup/recovery mechanism (optional passphrase)

  ---
  Phase 3: Enterprise Features (Priority 2)

  3.1 Advanced Permissions System
  - Add roles and permissions tables
  - Granular permissions:
    - channel.read, channel.write, channel.admin
    - channel.invite_users, channel.manage_members
    - channel.delete_messages, channel.pin_messages
    - org.create_channels, org.manage_users
  - API: Role assignment endpoints
  - UI: Permission management interface

  3.2 Message Pinning & Bookmarks
  - Add pinned_messages table (channel_id, message_id, pinned_by, pinned_at)
  - Add bookmarks table (user_id, message_id, bookmarked_at)
  - API:
    - POST /api/messages/{id}/pin
    - GET /api/channels/{id}/pins
    - POST /api/bookmarks
  - UI: Pin icon, pinned messages panel, personal bookmarks list

  3.3 Rich Text Formatting
  - Markdown support in message rendering
  - UI: WYSIWYG editor or markdown toolbar
  - Support: bold, italic, code blocks, lists, links, quotes
  - Preview mode before sending
  - Store as markdown in database

  3.4 Custom Emojis
  - Add custom_emojis table (org_id, name, image_url, created_by)
  - Upload flow: validate image, resize, store in S3
  - API: POST /api/emojis/upload, GET /api/emojis
  - UI: Emoji picker with org-specific emojis

  3.5 Message Reactions Enhancement
  - Support custom emoji reactions
  - Reaction aggregation and display optimization
  - Reaction notifications (optional per user)

  ---
  Phase 4: User Experience Enhancements (Priority 2)

  4.1 Advanced Status & Presence
  - Add user_status table (persist status messages)
  - Status types: online, away, do-not-disturb, offline
  - Custom status messages ("In a meeting", "On vacation")
  - Auto-away after inactivity (15 min default)
  - UI: Status picker, custom status input

  4.2 Read Receipts
  - Add message_read_receipts table
  - Track who read which message and when
  - UI: "Seen by" indicator (like Slack)
  - Privacy option: allow users to disable sending read receipts

  4.3 Message Drafts
  - Store unsent messages per channel/DM in client (IndexedDB)
  - Sync drafts across devices (optional, via API)
  - Auto-save every few seconds

  4.4 Keyboard Shortcuts
  - Cmd/Ctrl+K: Quick switcher (channels/DMs)
  - Cmd/Ctrl+F: Search messages
  - Up arrow: Edit last message
  - Cmd/Ctrl+Enter: Send message
  - Tab: Navigate channels
  - UI: Keyboard shortcuts help modal

  4.5 Message Editing History
  - Add message_edits table (message_id, old_content, edited_at, edited_by)
  - UI: "Edited" indicator with history viewer
  - API: GET /api/messages/{id}/history

  ---
  Phase 5: Collaboration Features (Priority 3)

  5.1 Voice/Video Calling
  - Integration options:
    - WebRTC with own signaling server
    - Jitsi Meet embedded
    - Daily.co API integration
  - Start with 1-on-1, expand to group calls
  - Screen sharing support

  5.2 Slash Commands
  - Add slash_commands table (name, description, handler_url, org_id)
  - Built-in commands: /giphy, /remind, /poll
  - Webhook support for custom commands
  - API: POST /api/commands/execute

  5.3 Message Reminders
  - Add reminders table (user_id, message_id, remind_at)
  - Background job to send notifications
  - UI: "Remind me about this" context menu

  5.4 Polls & Surveys
  - Add polls table (message_id, question, options_json, expires_at)
  - Add poll_votes table (poll_id, user_id, option_index)
  - Real-time vote updates via WebSocket
  - UI: Poll creation dialog, vote buttons, results chart

  5.5 Message Forwarding
  - UI: Forward message to another channel/DM
  - Preserve original sender info
  - API: POST /api/messages/{id}/forward

  ---
  Phase 6: Mobile & Integrations (Priority 3)

  6.1 Mobile Apps
  - React Native app (iOS + Android)
  - Share codebase with web where possible
  - Push notifications via FCM/APNS
  - Offline message queue

  6.2 Webhooks & Integrations
  - Add webhooks table (channel_id, url, events[], secret)
  - Outgoing webhooks for message events
  - Incoming webhooks for posting messages
  - API: Webhook CRUD endpoints

  6.3 Email Notifications
  - Background job for digest emails
  - User preferences: immediate, hourly, daily, never
  - Templates for mentions, DMs, thread replies

  6.4 Bots & API Tokens
  - Add bot_users table
  - API token generation for programmatic access
  - OAuth 2.0 for third-party apps
  - Rate limiting per token

  ---
  Phase 7: Performance & Scale (Priority 2 - Ongoing)

  7.1 Caching Strategy
  - Fully implement Redis cache modules (already scaffolded)
  - Cache patterns:
    - User sessions (5 min TTL)
    - Channel members (invalidate on change)
    - Recent messages (1 min TTL, paginated)
    - Unread counts (real-time updates)
  - Cache invalidation on mutations

  7.2 Database Optimization
  - Add indexes based on query patterns:
    - messages(channel_id, created_at DESC)
    - messages(dm_id, created_at DESC)
    - channel_members(user_id, channel_id)
    - mentions(user_id, created_at DESC)
  - Partitioning for messages table (by created_at)
  - Archive old messages (>1 year) to cold storage

  7.3 Rate Limiting
  - Add rate limiting middleware (redis-based)
  - Limits:
    - 5 messages/second per user
    - 20 API requests/second per user
    - 100 WebSocket messages/minute per connection
  - Return 429 with Retry-After header

  7.4 Monitoring & Observability
  - CloudWatch metrics for:
    - Message throughput
    - WebSocket connection count
    - API latency (p50, p95, p99)
    - Error rates
  - Distributed tracing (OpenTelemetry)
  - Alerting on critical failures

  7.5 CDN & Static Asset Optimization
  - Image optimization (WebP, lazy loading)
  - Code splitting for faster initial load
  - Service worker for offline support
  - Brotli compression

  ---
  Phase 8: Compliance & Security (Priority 2)

  8.1 Audit Logging
  - Add audit_logs table (user_id, action, resource_type, resource_id, metadata, timestamp)
  - Log all destructive actions:
    - Message deletion
    - Channel deletion
    - User removal
    - Permission changes
  - Retention policy (7 years for compliance)
  - API: Admin audit log viewer

  8.2 Data Retention Policies
  - Configurable per organization
  - Auto-delete messages after N days (optional)
  - Legal hold capability (freeze deletion for specific channels)
  - Export all data for GDPR compliance

  8.3 Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)
  - Enforce via TitaniumVault
  - Require for sensitive operations
  - Session timeout configuration

  8.4 Content Moderation
  - Profanity filter (optional, configurable)
  - Message reporting system
  - Admin message review queue
  - Auto-moderation rules

  ---
  Implementation Order Recommendation

  Sprint 1-2 (Weeks 1-4): Quick Wins

  1. Unread message tracking
  2. Thread UI display
  3. Message search (basic)
  4. File attachments (S3 setup)

  Sprint 3-5 (Weeks 5-10): E2E Encryption

  1. Crypto infrastructure (key management)
  2. Device registration
  3. Encryption/decryption implementation
  4. UI for encryption settings
  5. Testing & security audit

  Sprint 6-8 (Weeks 11-16): Core Features

  1. @Mentions & notifications
  2. Message pinning
  3. Rich text (Markdown)
  4. Advanced permissions
  5. Custom emojis

  Sprint 9-10 (Weeks 17-20): Polish & Performance

  1. Full caching implementation
  2. Rate limiting
  3. Database optimization
  4. Read receipts
  5. Keyboard shortcuts

  Sprint 11+ (Weeks 21+): Advanced Features

  1. Voice/video calling
  2. Slash commands
  3. Mobile apps
  4. Webhooks/integrations
  5. Audit logging

  ---
  Key Technical Decisions

  End-to-End Encryption:
  - Recommendation: Use Matrix Olm/Megolm protocol
    - Olm for 1-on-1 DMs (Double Ratchet)
    - Megolm for group channels (efficient group encryption)
    - Vodozemac crate for Rust backend
    - @matrix-org/olm for TypeScript frontend
    - Better group chat performance than Signal Protocol

  File Storage:
  - Recommendation: AWS S3 with CloudFront CDN
    - Pre-signed URLs for secure uploads
    - Lifecycle policies for cost optimization
    - Encryption at rest (S3-SSE or client-side)

  Search:
  - Recommendation: PostgreSQL full-text search (GIN index)
    - Simple, no extra infrastructure
    - Upgrade to Elasticsearch/MeiliSearch later if needed

  Voice/Video:
  - Recommendation: Start with Daily.co integration
    - Faster time-to-market
    - Built-in recording, screen sharing
    - Migrate to self-hosted Jitsi later if needed

  ---
  Questions for You

  1. Encryption Priority: Do you want E2E encryption from the start, or is it acceptable to add it in Phase 2 after core UX features?
  2. File Storage: Do you have an AWS S3 bucket preference, or should I set up a new dedicated bucket for openchat?
  3. Voice/Video: Third-party integration (Daily.co, Jitsi) or build WebRTC from scratch?
  4. Mobile Apps: Should I plan for React Native, or native Swift/Kotlin apps?
  5. Feature Priorities: Any features from the plan you want to prioritize or deprioritize?

  Let me know your thoughts and I can start implementing! I'll wait for your direction before making any code changes.

